WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.432
After cleaning data, we usually need to summarize it.

00:00:03.432 --> 00:00:08.772
In this second part of the mini project, we start with a cleaned list of orders.

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:16.617
The total_revenue function adds the amount for records where the status is complete.

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:20.017
The count_by_status function counts how many records have a particular status.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:24.027
Then we use assert statements to check important behavior.

00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:29.302
We expect the total revenue to be one hundred seventeen point five zero,

00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:32.277
and we expect two complete orders.

00:00:32.277 --> 00:00:39.302
If those checks pass, the program prints the revenue, the count, and Project checks passed.

00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:42.772
This example connects cleaning, summarizing, and testing.

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:48.097
The tests are small, but they protect the main business logic.

00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:54.792
If someone changes the function later and breaks the calculation, the assertion can catch the issue quickly.
